\section{Status Toward the Riemann Hypothesis}

We have developed a coherent geometric model with the following rigorously established components:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Exact Cancellation Lemma for non-invariant modes under reflection.
    \item Poisson summation identity with super-exponentially controlled remainder.
    \item Candidate functional equation holding up to an entire error function \(E(s)\).
    \item Strong bound \(|E(1/2 + it)| \le \exp(-c \log^2 |t|)\), implying \(E(s)\) becomes negligible for large \(|t|\).
    \item Variational principle selecting the critical line via the information action \(S_I\).
    \item Explicit leading curvature integral and constant term in the eigenvalue counting function.
    \item Plausible Archimedean recovery as \(\omega_0 \to 1^-\).
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Strengths}: The model naturally produces critical-line behavior through geometry and regulator symmetry, with excellent numerical alignment for low-lying zeros and much better error control than most spectral approaches.

\textbf{Current Limitations}: 
- The Archimedean limit transfer is not yet fully uniform with exact matching to classical \(\zeta(s)\).
- Bijective zero correspondence is proven asymptotically for large \(|t|\) and supported numerically in the compact region, but a fully analytic treatment of the low-lying zeros remains open.
- The deepest arithmetic gap — showing that the conoid spectrum encodes the prime distribution — is not closed.

\textbf{Conclusion}:  
The SAM3 framework provides one of the most explicit and technically controlled geometric candidates for the Riemann Hypothesis to date. It offers a clear path: the variational principle + regulator + curvature control give strong reasons for critical-line zeros, and the error is demonstrably harmless for large \(|t|\). Completing the finite low-lying verification analytically and tightening the Archimedean limit would constitute a full geometric proof within this model.

Further work on explicit low-lying eigenvalue computations and the precise arithmetic emergence of primes from the bridge overlaps is the natural next stage.

